      "text": "A lot of people pushed back on my take, and I appreciated their feedback.\n\nThe most reasonable explanation I heard was that Lumentum’s CEO was never really equipped to take the company to the next level. He previously spent just 1.5 years at FNSR before selling the company. His career has essentially been about growing companies to a certain point and then selling them.\n\nBy that logic, having driven an 18-fold increase in Lumentum’s share price in just 20 months and now sold the company, Hurlston has done his job.\n\nStill, it’s incredibly disappointing to see Lumentum give up on growing independently and choose to sell itself. It feels cowardly.",
